<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n69401" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μυρτίδᾰνον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a myrtle-like plant</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				1.34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>warty excrescence on the stem of the myrtle</i>,
			like the kermes berries on the holm-oak, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.112
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				23.164
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>seed of the Persian pepper-tree</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Mul.</u>
				2.205
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.106
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> an Indian or
			Persian fruit used as pepper, <i><span class="en">
				Diosc.Gloss.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i> l.c.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
